  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Утро пришло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Morning has come.' 'Morning' is neuter, so 'came' finishes with 'o'. A short, quiet start.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Теперь все ясно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now everything is clear.' 'Clear' is a word with an 'o' ending, used without a subject. There's no 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Но уже поздно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But it's already late.' 'Late' is a word with an 'o' ending. 'But already' are two small words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Время ушло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Time has gone.' 'Time' is neuter, so 'went away' carries 'o'. A very short sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это наша общая ошибка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's our common mistake.' 'Common' means 'shared'. 'Mistake' is feminine, so both words end in 'aya'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Может быть, стоило проснуться?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maybe we should have woken up?' The word 'stoilo' means 'it was worth'. 'Wake up' finishes with 'sya'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Проснуться раньше?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Woken up sooner?' 'Earlier' is just one word. Max repeats the idea.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я не знаю ответ.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't know the answer.' 'Answer' is a masculine word with no ending. 'I know' finishes with 'u'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Никто не знает.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody knows.' 'Nobody' and 'not' appear together. Two words and a full stop.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Жизнь продолжается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Life goes on.' 'Continues' carries 'sya', meaning it continues by itself. 'Life' ends in a soft sign.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Нужно идти.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We need to go.' 'Necessary' plus the plain 'to go'. It is a short instruction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Идти только вперед.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only forward.' 'Only' sits in front of 'forward'. The episode ends on the plain word. Now the whole conversation once more, from start to finish.",
